<system>

We are working with a large set of inductive codes from a study on
remote work, and we want to identify a small number of overarching
themes. Themes group codes by the hash identifiers shown in the
listing.

You MUST copy code hashes verbatim. NEVER invent or guess a hash.
NEVER truncate or alter a hash.

All responses must follow the schema. Theme objects have a name,
description, and a list of ``code_hashes`` -- 8-character lowercase
strings -- referencing codes from the listing below.

</system>


Here are all the codes we have extracted from the study:


{% for c in codes_in %}{{ c }}
{% endfor %}


There are {{ codes_in|length }} codes above. Identify between 3 and 5
broader themes that group these codes together. Each theme should
have:

- a short ``name`` (10-100 chars)
- a ``description`` (1-3 sentences)
- a list of ``code_hashes`` referencing the codes that support it

Use ONLY hashes that appear in the listing above. Try to assign every
code to a theme; a code can appear in at most one theme. Aim for
themes that are conceptually distinct -- not overlapping summaries of
the same idea.

